{
  "description": "Nested one-, two-, and four-camera representative traces for decomposing capture-worker CPU scaling residuals.",
  "notes": [
    "All cases use the same 30 FPS depth-plus-color profile and the same D455 as camera 0.",
    "The two-camera set is a subset of the four-camera set so device identity is not confounded with camera count.",
    "Use with LiME, V4L2 diagnostics, and the overrun kernel trace on the Raspberry Pi RT/UVC16 kernel."
